In mathematics, the <b>Laplace operator</b> or <b>Laplacian</b> is a differential operator given by the divergence of the gradient of a scalar function on Euclidean space. It is usually denoted by the symbols <span class="mwe-math-element"><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle 
